Description: Use fmt library instead of std::format for GCC 12 compatibility
 The upstream code uses C++20 <format> header which is not available
 in GCC 12's libstdc++. This patch replaces all usages of std::format,
 std::formatter, and #include <format> with their fmt library
 equivalents, since libfmt-dev is already a build dependency.
 .
 This is a mechanical replacement:
 - #include <format> -> #include <fmt/format.h>
 - std::format(...) -> fmt::format(...)
 - std::formatter<T> -> fmt::formatter<T>
 - formatter<T> (in std::formatter context) -> fmt::formatter<T>
Author: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
